This distribution includes protocol definitions derived from RustDesk and
binary/source components from FreeRDP, OpenSSL, FFmpeg, libssh2, Mbed TLS,
Opus, the platform zlib library, Huawei/OpenHarmony SDK packages, and Rust crates including the Apache-2.0 Alacritty terminal core. No project license
statement removes or replaces their upstream notices.

Debug builds additionally include libfido2 1.17.0 and libcbor 0.14.0 for the
explicitly authorized USB capability probe. Their source archives, local
custom-I/O patch, per-ABI manifests and full upstream notices are identified
in docs/compliance/FIDO2_OHOS_PROVENANCE.md and libs/fido2-ohos/. They are
excluded from Release native linking.

The separately deployable Pro entitlement server sources use external Node.js
and OpenSSL host runtimes. They are not bundled in the HAP or redistributed in
the server source directory. Runtime scope, validation versions and upstream
notices are recorded in server/pro-entitlement/PROVENANCE.md and its SBOM.
The private AGC deployment additionally packages a separately verified static
OpenSSL executable with musl and the GCC runtime. Its manifest, separate SBOM,
full upstream notices and build provenance are in server/pro-entitlement/agc/pkix/.
That executable and private deployment archive are not committed or bundled in the HAP.

The optional AGC deployment uses the Huawei Cloud Server SDK and locked npm
dependencies. Their separate SBOM and full notices are in
server/pro-entitlement/agc/. These dependencies are not included in the HAP.
